WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:12.420
Without warning, the children landed at the bottom of a tunnel with a loud thud.

2
00:00:12.421 --> 00:00:15.614
“Ouch!” shouted Vinnie.

3
00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:18.282
“Oomph!” cried Mandy.

4
00:00:18.283 --> 00:00:20.742
They opened their eyes.

5
00:00:20.743 --> 00:00:23.223
The bright light was gone.

6
00:00:23.224 --> 00:00:26.181
The darkness of the tunnel was gone, too.

7
00:00:26.182 --> 00:00:30.417
They both lay on the ground, not far from each other.

8
00:00:30.418 --> 00:00:34.613
“Are you okay?” Vinnie called to his sister.

9
00:00:34.614 --> 00:00:37.967
They had landed on the bank of a long river.

10
00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:41.069
They could see ducks and geese flying by.

11
00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:45.954
Men with nets and spears were fishing from boats and from land.

12
00:00:45.955 --> 00:00:49.619
“Mandy?” Vinnie called to her again.

13
00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:56.130
As he got up and moved closer to Mandy, Vinnie could see why she didn’t answer.

14
00:00:56.131 --> 00:01:00.095
Standing in front of her was a boy about Vinnie’s age.

15
00:01:00.096 --> 00:01:03.958
He was dark and slender.

16
00:01:03.959 --> 00:01:06.348
“Are you the gods of the Nile?”

17
00:01:06.348 --> 00:01:09.207
the boy asked, falling to his knees.

18
00:01:09.208 --> 00:01:12.271
“The Nile?” Vinnie questioned.

19
00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.868
Then he realized where they were.

20
00:01:14.869 --> 00:01:18.500
“We’re in Egypt!” he shouted at Mandy.

21
00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:20.818
“Please don’t hurt me,”

22
00:01:20.818 --> 00:01:24.152
the strange boy cried, his voice shaking.

23
00:01:24.153 --> 00:01:28.602
“No, we are not gods,” Vinnie said to the boy.

24
00:01:28.603 --> 00:01:32.410
“I’m Vinnie and this is my sister, Mandy.”

25
00:01:32.411 --> 00:01:38.874
The stranger wore only a short white skirt, tied with a sash around his waist.

26
00:01:38.875 --> 00:01:42.545
Suddenly Vinnie looked down at himself.

27
00:01:42.546 --> 00:01:45.430
That’s all he was wearing, too!

28
00:01:45.431 --> 00:01:47.925
Vinnie’s face turned red.

29
00:01:47.926 --> 00:01:51.087
Mandy was also dressed differently.

30
00:01:51.088 --> 00:01:54.805
Her body was covered by a straight white dress.

31
00:01:54.806 --> 00:01:57.240
Her feet were in sandals.

32
00:01:57.241 --> 00:01:59.739
Her hair was in a long braid.

33
00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:02.707
“But I saw you fall from the sky,”

34
00:02:02.708 --> 00:02:06.217
said the boy, getting back up on his feet.

35
00:02:06.218 --> 00:02:12.049
“We have . . . special powers,” she paused and looked at Vinnie.

36
00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:16.873
He was still holding the photograph, which he stuck inside his sash.

37
00:02:16.874 --> 00:02:20.733
The stranger gasped and fell to his knees again.

38
00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:25.940
“Don’t worry. We’re not going to hurt you,” Mandy said kindly.

39
00:02:25.941 --> 00:02:28.253
“We need your help.”

40
00:02:28.254 --> 00:02:33.572
“I am Akhom,” the boy said, “and I promise to help you.”

41
00:02:33.573 --> 00:02:36.677
“Thank you, Akhom,” said Mandy.

42
00:02:36.678 --> 00:02:40.935
They heard voices coming toward them from the distance.

43
00:02:40.936 --> 00:02:43.480
Vinnie and Mandy froze.

44
00:02:43.481 --> 00:02:47.668
“Oh, those are my friends,” Akhom explained.

45
00:02:47.669 --> 00:02:51.269
He held up an odd shaped ball in his hand.

46
00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.531
“I left them to look for my ball.

47
00:02:53.532 --> 00:02:55.947
Then I saw you.”

48
00:02:55.948 --> 00:02:59.074
Vinnie and Mandy looked at each other.

49
00:02:59.075 --> 00:03:03.606
“Please don’t tell them about us, Akhom,” they both said.

50
00:03:03.607 --> 00:03:07.745
Akhom nodded. “Yes, it would be best for you to hide.

51
00:03:07.746 --> 00:03:10.935
My friends are not accustomed to strangers.”

52
00:03:10.936 --> 00:03:13.948
The loud shouts came nearer.

53
00:03:13.949 --> 00:03:19.350
“Akhom! Are you looking for cobras again?” shouted one boy.

54
00:03:19.351 --> 00:03:22.403
“Cobras?” whispered Vinnie.

55
00:03:22.404 --> 00:03:26.679
Vinnie hated snakes even more than spiders.

56
00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.717
“Cobras, hippos, crocodiles.

57
00:03:29.718 --> 00:03:34.074
They’re all over the Nile,” Akhom whispered back.

58
00:03:34.075 --> 00:03:40.718
“Crocodiles!” Vinnie mouthed, his eyes getting very big.

59
00:03:40.719 --> 00:03:46.215
“Akhom! Where are you?” the voices shouted again .

60
00:03:46.216 --> 00:03:50.142
Akhom threw the ball back to his friends.

61
00:03:50.143 --> 00:03:53.353
Then he signaled to Vinnie and Mandy.

62
00:03:53.354 --> 00:03:57.217
“Quickly follow me!”

63
00:03:57.218 --> 00:04:01.745
Vinnie and Mandy ran after him.

64
00:04:01.746 --> 00:04:07.619
Out of breath, they arrived at a small house with windows high up on the walls.

65
00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:11.478
Its white surface had many cracks from the hot sun.

66
00:04:11.479 --> 00:04:17.531
“Welcome to my home,” Akhom said warmly.
